# CRITICAL GAME OVERHAUL: CHARACTER INTELLIGENCE, COMMAND OBEDIENCE, MYSTERY & EMERGENT DRAMA

## PROJECT INSTRUCTION

The current game's visual atmosphere and presentation are acceptable. However, its simulation intelligence is severely underdeveloped.

Characters wander around without meaningful purposes, ignore or misinterpret player instructions, repeat meaningless conversations, have no convincing personalities, and generate almost no suspense, mystery, conflict, or unexpected behaviour.

**This is a critical gameplay-system overhaul.**

Do not waste time redesigning the visual identity, replacing existing environments, or adding decorative features.

Preserve all functioning visual systems, characters, animations, environments, interface elements, and existing gameplay features.

Your priority is to transform the existing characters into believable autonomous individuals who can understand commands, execute plans, respond intelligently, remember experiences, and develop their own stories.

Do not simply add more random animations or dialogue.

Rebuild the underlying intelligence.

